{"content":[{"c":["ABDON (P",{"c":["erson"],"sourceClass":"lc","t":"span"},")"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Hillel’s son who judged Israel for eight years (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.12.13-15","r":"Judg.12.13-15","rawR":"Judg.12.13-15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.12.13-15","value":"Judg.12.13-15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 12:13-15"},"). Abdon was a very wealthy man, as indicated by reference to the 70 donkeys he owned."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Shashak’s son from Benjamin’s tribe who lived in Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.23,28","r":"1Chr.8.23,28","rawR":"1Chr.8.23,28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.23,28","value":"1Chr.8.23,28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:23, 28"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Jeiel’s oldest son from Benjamin’s tribe who lived in Gibeon. This Abdon is mentioned in Saul’s genealogy (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.8.30","r":"1Chr.8.30","rawR":"1Chr.8.30","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.8.30","value":"1Chr.8.30"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 8:30"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.9.36","r":"1Chr.9.36","rawR":"1Chr.9.36","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.9.36","value":"1Chr.9.36"}],"t":"ref","v":"9:36"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Micah’s son (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.34.20","r":"2Chr.34.20","rawR":"2Chr.34.20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.34.20","value":"2Chr.34.20"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 34:20"},"), also called Acbor, son of Micaiah. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Acbor_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Acbor_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Acbor_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Acbor #2"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AbdonPerson","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 12:13-15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.12.13-15","rawQueryValue":"Judg.12.13